  "report": "# Phase 3 isolated OCI verification and exact remaining blockers\n\nStatus: B1_P3_BLOCKED. No complete acceptance claim.\n\nFinal source: 9d6234afdd0a20e99f584acf7f93e346c5c49164. Accepted software d750836bfa44bd6fa668f827a4529ed49dec5269 and its authenticated evidence are preserved. All 22 original criteria, 12 action classes, 20 bindings and the evaluator remain unchanged.\n\n## Verified\n\n- One Always Free standard OCI Vault and one SOFTWARE AES-256 key in me-dubai-1. Two retained enabled versions. No paid private vault, compute resource, billing upgrade, permanent API key, new IAM grant, live credential migration or production change.\n- Additive OCI CryptoProvider uses the existing canonical CredentialVault, exact identity/AAD binding, bounded provider requests and explicit short-lived authentication. Twelve focused provider/vault tests passed and backend typecheck passed.\n- Nine isolated provider cases and nineteen retained OCI request IDs cover real wrap/unwrap, wrong AAD, unavailable key, unsigned rejection, canonical vault identity negatives, version rotation and retained-version recovery after process restart. Signed operator access is not application IAM proof.\n- Ten of eleven final-source workflows passed. Both 21-stage branch baselines passed twice: backend 3128/3128, frontend 1051/1051. Actual disposable database authorization/concurrency 209/209, authenticated browser and fresh/upgrade migrations passed.\n- The exact integrated parent identities and artifacts were authenticated. Its provenance preflight passed after the bounded native Array.from false-positive projection repair. No security review was waived.\n- Provider receipts are durably attached to OCI implementation source 2e7dd1ec via Git notes, leaving the original d750836b note unchanged. This final bundle preserves current-source results separately.\n\n## Remaining integrated CI requirement\n\nRun 39493219759, integrated source c5ffc1c30866dc2af36fb371c80a83111806d887, actual