solated synthetic custody/cutover. Cloud Shell success and unsigned HTTP401 denial do not replace those tests. No administrator token may be installed into the backend. Any new IAM trust/grant requires the applicable action-time owner confirmation. No paid resource is needed by the completed crypto probe. Cost of an unconfigured future identity path must be confirmed before creating it.\n\nBoth SOFTWARE key versions remain enabled. OCI Vault backup does not support SOFTWARE keys. Process-restart recovery is not key backup or disaster-recovery proof. Keep the original key and last decrypt-capable principal. Do not disable, delete or export keys.\n\n## Strict gate\n\nThe unchanged --evidence/--observations/--require-complete gate was run against honest current-source observations. It exits 1 with Integrated CI is incomplete, before the separate mandatory runtime-custody check. It cannot truthfully report CODE_READY_KMS_CUTOVER_BLOCKED as the only current dependency while integrated CI is red.\n\nProcedure and full command: docs/xroga/evidence/command-009/oci-kms-procedure.md. No new spending, production deployment, merge, Google billing change, live migration or Phase 4.\n",
